Implemented Vercel Speed Insights for Next.js
===============================================

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js 16.1.0 application with App Router.

Changes Made:
-------------

1. **Installed @vercel/speed-insights package**
   - Used npm to install @vercel/speed-insights
   - Package added to dependencies in package.json
   - package-lock.json updated with new dependency tree

2. **Updated Root Layout (src/app/layout.tsx)**
   - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
   - Added <SpeedInsights /> component inside the <body> tag
   - Placed after the <Providers> component and before the Razorpay script
   - This ensures Speed Insights tracks all page navigations and interactions

Implementation Details:
-----------------------

- **Next.js Version**: 16.1.0 (supports App Router, version > 13.5)
- **Router Type**: App Router (modern Next.js setup)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Integration Type**: Used '@vercel/speed-insights/next' for optimal App Router support
- **Component Placement**: Inside <body> tag in root layout for application-wide tracking

Testing & Verification:
-----------------------

✓ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✓ No new linting errors introduced
✓ Dependencies properly installed and lock file updated
✓ All changes staged with git

The SpeedInsights component will now automatically track Core Web Vitals and performance metrics when the application is deployed to Vercel. No additional configuration is required - the component works out of the box with Vercel's infrastructure.

Files Modified:
---------------
- frontend/package.json (added @vercel/speed-insights dependency)
- frontend/package-lock.json (updated with new dependency tree)
- frontend/src/app/layout.tsx (added SpeedInsights import and component)
